`NGX_PEER_NEXT` is triggered when the upstream failure type is `NGX_HTTP_UPSTREAM_FT_HTTP_404`—that is, when `proxy_next_upstream http_404` applies:

```c
if (ft_type == NGX_HTTP_UPSTREAM_FT_HTTP_404) {
    state = NGX_PEER_NEXT;
} else {
    state = NGX_PEER_FAILED;
}
```

The cited nginx ticket describes this in the context of retrying after an upstream returns HTTP 404. The search results do not provide a complete list of other conditions that may trigger `NGX_PEER_NEXT`.
